-- title:
--   Selfmaps with weakly topologized values
-- statement:
--   These notions belong to a proof that every reflexive real Banach space has the fixed point property for nonexpansive maps: every $F:C\to C$ with $\|Fa-Fb\|\le\|a-b\|$ on a nonempty closed bounded convex set $C$ has a fixed point. The proof assumes a fixed-point-free map, reduces to a minimal invariant set $K$ of diameter $1$, builds an adaptive weighted tree of nonexpansive maps generated by resolvents, and contradicts the minimality through detecting functionals. Let $K\subseteq X$.
--
--   1. **Weak selfmaps.** Functions from $K$ (with its norm) to the weak carrier of $K$. Their space carries the product, i.e. pointwise weak, topology.
--   2. **Conversions.** $\mathrm{ofNorm}$ and $\mathrm{toNorm}$ identify weak selfmaps with ordinary selfmaps $K\to K$. The map $\mathrm{ofNorm}$ is continuous from pointwise norm to pointwise weak convergence.
--   3. **Composition.** $(f\circ g)(a)=f(\mathrm{toNorm}\,g(a))$, the composition of the underlying selfmaps. It is associative, and for fixed $g$ the right translation
--   $$
--   f\mapsto f\circ g
--   $$
--   is continuous, with no continuity assumption on $g$.
--   4. **Weakify.** The coordinatewise linear identification of $K\to X$ with $K\to X_{\mathrm{weak}}$.
